SUMMARY:Sebastian Cetina LIVE at Brea Improv
DESCRIPTION:Official Tickets \nAbout Sebastian Cetina\nSebastian Cetina is a uniquely gifted stand-up comedian\, host\, actor\, producer\, and impressionist who has spent over 21 years proving himself as one of the funniest and most versatile comedians in America. Sebastian headlines comedy clubs and colleges all over the U.S. and has become one of the most exciting and sought-after hosts in the business — currently serving as the host of Caliente Mondays at the World Famous Laugh Factory in Hollywood. His comedy style blends the character work of Eddie Murphy\, the loveable insults of Don Rickles\, the improv genius of Robin Williams\, and the audience interaction of Andrew Dice Clay. He can perform 100+ different impressions\, original characters\, and accents — from pop stars to presidents to cartoon characters — making every show a completely unique experience. \nWhat to Expect\nA Sebastian Cetina show is a non-stop\, high-energy comedy experience. Expect rapid-fire impressions\, hilarious characters\, and spontaneous audience interaction that keeps the crowd roaring from start to finish. Sebastian is known for his ability to improvise an entire 90-minute show on the spot\, reacting to the audience and the room in real time. His mass appeal means he can perform clean shows for all ages\, but at the Brea Improv (a 21+ venue)\, expect him to unleash his full\, unfiltered comedic arsenal. No two Sebastian Cetina shows are ever the same. \nAbout Brea Improv\nThe Brea Improv is one of Southern California’s premier comedy clubs\, located at 180 S Brea Blvd in Brea\, CA — just 30 miles southeast of downtown Los Angeles. Part of the nationally renowned Improv Comedy Club chain\, the Brea location features an intimate showroom with general admission seating\, premium booths\, and a full food and beverage menu. The club has a mandatory two-item minimum per guest in the showroom\, making it a true dinner-and-a-show experience. With its cozy atmosphere and excellent sightlines\, every seat feels close to the stage. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Wednesday\, July 15\, 2026\nTime: 8:00 PM PDT (Doors open at 6:30 PM)\nVenue: Brea Improv\, 180 S Brea Blvd\, Brea\, CA 92821\nAge Requirement: 21+\nTicket Prices: $25 – $75 (plus fees)\n\nOfficial Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
