SUMMARY:Conor Janda LIVE at Cobb's Comedy Club
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nConor Janda is a sharp\, witty stand-up comedian who has been making waves on the national comedy circuit with his clever writing and relatable storytelling. Known for his dry humor and self-deprecating style\, Janda has a gift for finding the absurdity in everyday life and turning it into laugh-out-loud material. \nA regular on the club circuit and a rising presence in the comedy world\, Conor Janda has earned a reputation as one of the most consistently funny performers working today. His sets are tight\, well-crafted\, and delivered with a natural ease that makes even the most complex observations feel effortless. \nWhether you’re a longtime fan or catching him for the first time\, Conor Janda’s show at Cobb’s Comedy Club promises to be a memorable night of stand-up comedy. \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, July 16\, 2026\nTime: 7:30 PM PDT\nVenue: Cobb’s Comedy Club\, 915 Columbus Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA 94133\nAge Restriction: 18+ / 2 Beverage Minimum\nTicket Price Range: $28 – $47 \nAbout the Venue\nCobb’s Comedy Club is one of San Francisco’s most iconic comedy destinations\, nestled in the vibrant North Beach neighborhood at 915 Columbus Avenue. With a capacity of approximately 400 guests\, the club delivers an intimate\, up-close experience that makes every seat feel like the best in the house. \nThe venue features a full bar and table service\, so you can enjoy cocktails\, beer\, wine\, and food throughout the performance. The classic comedy club layout — tables and chairs arranged around a central stage — ensures excellent sightlines and a communal atmosphere that amplifies the laughs. \nCobb’s is easily accessible by public transit and is surrounded by some of San Francisco’s best restaurants and bars\, making it a perfect spot for a full night out. Parking is available in nearby garages throughout the North Beach area. \nWhat to Expect\nThis is a solo stand-up performance by Conor Janda — a full evening of his signature observational and self-deprecating comedy. Expect a polished\, well-paced show with sharp writing and plenty of big laughs from start to finish. \nThe 18+ age restriction and 2-beverage minimum are in effect. Doors typically open 30–45 minutes before showtime\, so arrive early to get settled and enjoy a pre-show drink before the laughs kick off. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $28 – $47 (before taxes and fees)\nTickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) and VividSeats (resale). \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
